\title{One-to-one / injective}
\date{2026-03-10T10:33:56Z}
\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\taxon{Definition}
\p{A function #{f : A \to B} is \em{one-to-one} (\em{injective}, an \em{injection}) iff no two different elements of the domain map to the same element of the codomain. That is, ##{\forall a_1, a_2 \in A \st a_1 \neq a_2 \implies f(a_1) \neq f(a_2),}
 or equivalently, taking the contrapositive,
##{\forall a_1, a_2 \in A \st f(a_1) = f(a_2) \implies a_1 = a_2.}
}
